// @status: GENERAL
// @invariant: forbidden_effect
// @dimension: indirect invalid — reuse makes it wrong, not the kind
//
// Reuse is declared as `partition public` rather than `placement build` since
// 2026-08-11. Both make the output reused, and `reuse_of` reads either — but
// once UI declarations parsed their policies inside their braces the pinned
// world became VISIBLE to `declared_world`, and the placement solver added a
// second, correct diagnostic: `clock.wall` is not grantable at build time. A
// witness must exercise one invariant, and this one is about reuse.
//
// That the pin was previously invisible is the finding, and it is recorded in
// `docs/RISK_QUEUE.md`: `PW5005` could not fire for any page or component,
// because `placement` in a UI body was two unrelated bare names.
module generality.forbid_build_clock

import clock

page Landing() !{ clock.wall } {
    partition public
    view { <main><p>Generated at {clock.now_wall()}</p></main> }
}
